[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: 20 Function requirements

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: bench.sgra

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
Level 2: behaviour of the logical functions (see docs/architecture/logical/), still independent of the node a function runs on. Verified by integration tests against the HPC and the virtual twins. IDs: FUN-<AREA>-NNN. Each traces to a system requirement (SYS). Allocation to a node happens one level down.
<<<

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Indicator and hazard function

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FUN-LIGHT-001
STATUS: Draft
KIND: Functional
VERIFICATION: Test
MILESTONE: M1
TITLE: Indicator flashing
STATEMENT: >>>
When the left or the right indicator is requested and no hazard is requested, the indicator function shall flash only the requested side at 1.5 Hz with a 50 % duty cycle.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-LIGHT-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FUN-LIGHT-002
STATUS: Draft
KIND: Functional
VERIFICATION: Test
MILESTONE: M1
RELEVANCE: Safety
TITLE: Hazard priority
STATEMENT: >>>
While the hazard warning is requested, the indicator function shall flash both sides in phase, regardless of any left or right indicator request.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-LIGHT-002

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FUN-LIGHT-003
STATUS: Draft
KIND: Functional
VERIFICATION: Test
MILESTONE: M1
TITLE: Invalid indicator combination
STATEMENT: >>>
If the left and the right indicator are requested at the same time without a hazard request, the indicator function shall flash neither side.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Open question from spec 002 (to be settled in /speckit-clarify): confirm this behaviour.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-LIGHT-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FUN-LIGHT-010
STATUS: Draft
KIND: Functional
VERIFICATION: Test
TITLE: Comfort blink
STATEMENT: >>>
When the driver taps a direction request for less than 0.5 s, the indicator function shall flash the selected side the coded number of times (default 3).
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Lane-change convenience; the number of flashes is market-specific (variant coding).
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Node allocation not decided yet (stalk input on the HPC or edge logic on the ZC-STM32); no component requirement exists until it is.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-LIGHT-003

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Low beam function

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FUN-LIGHT-004
STATUS: Draft
KIND: Functional
VERIFICATION: Test
MILESTONE: M1
TITLE: Low beam switching
STATEMENT: >>>
While low beam is requested, the low beam function shall keep the low beam on; otherwise it shall keep it off.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-LIGHT-004

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Fail-safe and fault reporting

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FUN-SAFE-001
STATUS: Draft
KIND: Functional
VERIFICATION: Test
MILESTONE: M1
RELEVANCE: Safety
TITLE: Command-loss fail-safe
STATEMENT: >>>
If no valid light command has been received for 500 ms or longer, the lighting functions shall switch the indicators off, switch the low beam on and report a degraded state; when valid commands return, they shall resume normal behaviour automatically.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Low beam on keeps the vehicle visible; indicators off avoids signalling a direction nobody requested. The 500 ms timeout is five missed 100 ms command cycles (ADR 0002).
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-SAFE-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FUN-DIAG-001
STATUS: Draft
KIND: Functional
VERIFICATION: Test
MILESTONE: M1
TITLE: Actual state and fault reporting
STATEMENT: >>>
The lighting functions shall report their actual lamp states, their operating state and detected faults to the rest of the vehicle and to diagnostic access.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-DIAG-001

[[/SECTION]]
